emit-note-outcomes-through-app-server

Lane: mixed

Unit: present-note-operations-in-context-management

ChildPatch: emit-note-outcomes-through-app-server

Form: GitDiff

Segment: schema-snapshot

Purpose: Show every completed context-management note operation as routine or failure feedback in the TUI conversation.

Requires: none

Provides: Emit typed thread-scoped notices for successful note listing, reads, searches, appends, writes and automatic note-reference loading. Render each success as a normal bullet without warning entries. Preserve visible attention-colored failure bullets and warning details. Reuse native extension delivery, listener ordering and subscriber readiness for both outcomes.

Boundary: Disabled operations and history tools remain silent. Note contents, paths, queries and raw backend errors are not disclosed. Model-facing results, analytics, cancellation and ordinary warning semantics remain unchanged. Routine notices are transient TUI feedback rather than durable history or exec errors. The complete formal Unit remains independent of draft and private frontend responsibilities.

Verification: The installed history-notes extension tests cover every successful and failed action, repeated actions, empty reference results, disabled loading and unchanged model-facing output. App-server checks cover notification encoding, FIFO delivery, subscriber routing and existing warning behavior. TUI checks cover startup and runtime, fullscreen and legacy views, repeated normal bullets, raw and compact visibility, warning separation and thread targeting.


